  "name": "copernicus-fire-danger-forecast",
  "notes": "The fire danger forecast provides daily fire danger indices. The continuous raster\nGeoTIFFs in this dataset are from the ECMWF (~8 km) and NASA Geos-5 (~28 km) models.\n\nThe Fire Weather Index (FWI) is computed from the ECMWF and NASA Geos-5 models.\nThe FWI is mapped in 6 classes: low, medium, high, very high, extreme and very extreme.\nThe \"Very Extreme\" class was introduced in June 2021 to discriminate against\nextensive areas initially classified at \"Extreme\" in the Mediterranean region\nduring summer months, and includes areas with FWI values above 70.",
